# x-release-please-start-version
PRINT """
Inux v2.0.0 — Vinod Liyanage

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `/inux help` | Show commands. |
| `/inux setup` | Set up tools and sign in. |
| `/inux task <id>` | Load a Jira ticket into conversation context. |
| `/inux branch create` | Create and switch to a local task branch. |
| `/inux commit changes` | Stage intended changes and create a local commit. |
| `/inux estimate [request]` | Create an empty template, improve, generate, or publish to Jira. |
| `/inux ts [request]` | Generate, improve, publish, or finish a technical summary. |
| `/inux technical summary [request]` | Alias for `/inux ts [request]`. |
| `/inux pr [request]` | Prepare, refine, explain, publish, or finish a PR. |

Bare `/inux estimate` creates and opens an empty temporary estimate template.
Add a sentence to create a template, improve it, generate it completely, or publish
to Jira. The agent infers the intention from that sentence.
For ts and pr, `[request]` is required. Unsupported, conflicting, or ambiguous
requests show a usage error and stop.

Drafts are temporary Markdown files outside your repository, created only when
requested. Edit them directly or with the agent. Verified publication removes the
selected draft; `/inux ts done` or `/inux pr done` removes that draft without
publishing. Failed publication keeps the draft.

Examples: `/inux estimate improve the reasons`, `/inux ts summarize these changes`,
`/inux pr improve the title`.

Publishing requires an explicit `/inux estimate publish`,
`/inux ts publish` (or `/inux technical summary publish`), or `/inux pr publish` request.
"""
# x-release-please-end
